IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-homicide`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-homicide.l4 (sections 4, 5,
-- 9, 10 and the "text does not say" answers).  Every expected value was decided from
-- the text of the section before the assertion was written, and is stated beside it.

§ `Tests: homicide`

§§ `Section 4`

-- Columns of `Conduct under section 4`, in DECLARE order (the ruler is load-bearing:
-- OF is positional).
--   solicited, encouraged, persuaded, endeavoured to persuade, proposed,
--   what was put would be a murder, other is a subject, other within the dominions
`s4 solicited` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s4 encouraged` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s4 persuaded` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s4 endeavoured only` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s4 proposed` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s4 did none of the five` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s4 proposed something that would not be a murder` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
-- the two facts about the other person that the text says do not matter, flipped
`s4 proposed, other not a subject, not within the dominions` MEANS `Conduct under section 4` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Each of the five verbs, alone, with a murder in view, is the offence.
#ASSERT `s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 solicited`
#ASSERT `s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 encouraged`
#ASSERT `s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 persuaded`
#ASSERT `s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 endeavoured only`
#ASSERT `s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 proposed`
-- None of the five verbs: nothing in the section is met.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 did none of the five`)
-- The thing put to the person must be a murder ("to murder any other person").
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 proposed something that would not be a murder`)
-- "whether he be a subject of Her Majesty or not, and whether he be within the Queen's
-- dominions or not": flipping both facts changes nothing.
#ASSERT `s 4: soliciting or proposing a murder` `s4 proposed, other not a subject, not within the dominions`
-- The text calls it a misdemeanor and states imprisonment for life.
#ASSERT `s 4: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 4: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` `for life`

§§ `Section 5`

-- A conviction of manslaughter: the text states penal servitude for life.
#ASSERT `s 5: the sentences the text states for a conviction of manslaughter` TRUE EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`
-- No conviction: the section states nothing that follows.
#ASSERT `s 5: the sentences the text states for a conviction of manslaughter` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
-- The section does not classify the offence.
#ASSERT `s 5: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS `no classification stated`

§§ `What the text does not say: murder and manslaughter (outside the encoding)`

-- Sections 1 and 2 are rows of dots and section 5 gives no element: the text does not
-- answer "is it a murder?" or "is it a manslaughter?".  Asserted as the explicit value.
#ASSERT `whether what happened is a murder, as this text defines murder` EQUALS `the deposited text does not say`
#ASSERT `whether what happened is a manslaughter, as this text defines manslaughter` EQUALS `the deposited text does not say`

§§ `Section 9`

-- Columns of `Killing abroad under section 9`:
--   a murder or manslaughter was committed, on land out of the UK, the person charged
--   is a subject, the place is within the dominions, the person killed was a subject,
--   the killing was out of England or Ireland
`s9 the standard case` MEANS `Killing abroad under section 9` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s9 charged is not a subject` MEANS `Killing abroad under section 9` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s9 not on land` MEANS `Killing abroad under section 9` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s9 neither murder nor manslaughter` MEANS `Killing abroad under section 9` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
-- the two facts the text says do not matter: outside the dominions, victim not a subject
`s9 outside the dominions, victim not a subject` MEANS `Killing abroad under section 9` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s9 killing was in England` MEANS `Killing abroad under section 9` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 9: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s9 the standard case`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s9 charged is not a subject`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s9 not on land`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s9 neither murder nor manslaughter`)
-- "whether within the Queen's dominions or without, and whether the person killed were
-- a subject of Her Majesty or not": still the same answer.
#ASSERT `s 9: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s9 outside the dominions, victim not a subject`
-- The proviso: a trial out of England or Ireland is not prevented where the killing was
-- out of England or Ireland, and the proviso is silent where it was in England.
#ASSERT `s 9: a trial out of England or Ireland is not prevented by this Act` `s9 the standard case`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9: a trial out of England or Ireland is not prevented by this Act` `s9 killing was in England`)

§§ `Section 10`

-- Columns of `Hurt and death under section 10`:
--   hurt criminally, where hurt, died of the hurt, where died, amounts to murder or manslaughter
`s10 hurt at sea, died in England` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `upon the sea`, TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE
`s10 hurt abroad on land, died in Ireland` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `at a place out of England or Ireland, other than the sea`, TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE
`s10 hurt in England, died at sea` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE, `upon the sea`, TRUE
`s10 hurt in England, died abroad on land` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE, `at a place out of England or Ireland, other than the sea`, TRUE
`s10 hurt and died in England` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE
`s10 hurt at sea, died abroad on land` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `upon the sea`, TRUE, `at a place out of England or Ireland, other than the sea`, TRUE
`s10 hurt at sea, did not die` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `upon the sea`, FALSE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE
`s10 not criminally hurt` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF FALSE, `upon the sea`, TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, TRUE
`s10 not murder or manslaughter` MEANS `Hurt and death under section 10` OF TRUE, `upon the sea`, TRUE, `in England or Ireland`, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 hurt at sea, died in England`
#ASSERT `s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 hurt abroad on land, died in Ireland`
#ASSERT `s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 hurt in England, died at sea`
#ASSERT `s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 hurt in England, died abroad on land`
-- both in England: the section does not reach it (it needs no help from s 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 hurt and died in England`)
-- both out: the section reaches only a death or its cause in England or Ireland
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 hurt at sea, died abroad on land`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 hurt at sea, did not die`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 not criminally hurt`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10: the person may be dealt with, tried and punished in England or Ireland` `s10 not murder or manslaughter`)
